<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; History by century</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: The 20th century</h1><p class="ws-lede">A worksheet on the 1900s: the states, events and people of the century. Use its page to find the answers.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/centuries/20th-century">Open the century page &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><p class="ws-how">Each number marks the capital or seat of a state that existed in 1950 CE. Write its name from the word bank on the line with the same number.</p><figure class="ws-mapfig"><svg class="map map-world ws-map" viewBox="0 0 11581 6095" role="img" aria-label="Map: 8 numbered states of the world in 1950 CE"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><g class="ws-pins"><g><circle cx="2570" cy="1008" r="197"/><text x="2570" y="1091" font-size="236">1</text></g><g><circle cx="4997" cy="651" r="197"/><text x="4997" y="733" font-size="236">2</text></g><g><circle cx="5820" cy="533" r="197"/><text x="5820" y="616" font-size="236">3</text></g><g><circle cx="3203" cy="831" r="197"/><text x="3203" y="914" font-size="236">4</text></g><g><circle cx="8774" cy="3709" r="197"/><text x="8774" y="3792" font-size="236">5</text></g><g><circle cx="8221" cy="1549" r="197"/><text x="8221" y="1632" font-size="236">6</text></g><g><circle cx="6029" cy="1964" r="197"/><text x="6029" y="2047" font-size="236">7</text></g><g><circle cx="7959" cy="2664" r="197"/><text x="7959" y="2747" font-size="236">8</text></g></g></svg><figcaption>The world in 1950 CE</figcaption></figure><p class="ws-bank"><b>Word bank:</b> Canada &middot; Republic of China &middot; United States &middot; Ethiopian Empire &middot; Commonwealth of Australia &middot; British Empire &middot; Soviet Union &middot; Indonesia</p><ol class="ws-blanks"><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li></ol></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the events from 1 (earliest) to 6 (latest).</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Holocaust</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Great Depression</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Armistice of 11 November 1918</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Cold War</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Treaty of Vereeniging</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Korean War</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><p class="ws-how">Write the number of the right dates next to each person. Look them up in the encyclopedia.</p><div class="ws-match"><ol class="ws-ma" type="A"><li>Mikhail Gorbachev</li><li>Adolf Hitler</li><li>Bảo Đại</li><li>Joseph Stalin</li><li>George V</li><li>Milton Obote</li></ol><ol class="ws-mb"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1878–1953</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1865–1936</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1925–2005</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1913–1997</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1889–1945</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1931–2022</li></ol></div></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Key terms</h2><p class="ws-how">These words appear in the entries of this century. Explain each one in your own words.</p><ul class="ws-terms"><li><b>Genocide</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><b>German Emperor</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><b>Kabaka of Buganda</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">5</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p>In the 1900s, 518 recorded states were founded and 1,166 came to an end. Choose one of each from the century page. What happened to them?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>The great powers of the age included the United States, the British Empire and the Soviet Union. Choose one: what made it strong in these hundred years, and what threatened it?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Choose one event from the list and one person. How might they be connected? Use the encyclopedia to find out.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>If you could visit one place in the 20th century, where would you go, and what would you hope to see?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/centuries/20th-century. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: The 20th century</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>United States <span>1776 CE – present</span></li><li>British Empire <span>1583 CE – 1997 CE</span></li><li>Soviet Union <span>1922 CE – 1991 CE</span></li><li>Canada <span>1867 CE – present</span></li><li>Commonwealth of Australia <span>1901 CE – present</span></li><li>Republic of China <span>1912 CE – present</span></li><li>Ethiopian Empire <span>1270 CE – 1974 CE</span></li><li>Indonesia <span>1945 CE – present</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Treaty of Vereeniging <span>1902</span></li><li>Armistice of 11 November 1918 <span>1918</span></li><li>Great Depression <span>1929–1939</span></li><li>Holocaust <span>1941–1945</span></li><li>Cold War <span>1947–1991</span></li><li>Korean War <span>1950–1953</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><ol class="ws-key-list" type="A"><li>Mikhail Gorbachev <span>6: 1931–2022</span></li><li>Adolf Hitler <span>5: 1889–1945</span></li><li>Bảo Đại <span>4: 1913–1997</span></li><li>Joseph Stalin <span>1: 1878–1953</span></li><li>George V <span>2: 1865–1936</span></li><li>Milton Obote <span>3: 1925–2005</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Key terms</h2><dl class="ws-key-terms"><dt>Genocide</dt><dd>Genocide is the deliberate destruction of a national, ethnic, racial or religious group.</dd><dt>German Emperor</dt><dd>German Emperor was the title of the head of the German Empire from 1871 to 1918, always held by the King of Prussia.</dd><dt>Kabaka of Buganda</dt><dd>The Kabaka of Buganda is the title of the king of Buganda, the largest of the traditional kingdoms in present-day Uganda.</dd></dl></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">5</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers name states, people and events from the century page.</p></section></div></details>
